## 🌟 Overview

AsohCloak is the security backbone for a future School Management platform, built first as a **standalone, deeply-understood auth system**. Every credential, token, and access-control decision is delegated to **Keycloak** — AsohCloak itself never stores a password or manually signs a token. This project doubles as a hands-on reference implementation for combining Spring Boot's OAuth2 Resource Server support with Keycloak's Admin API and custom SPI extensions for flows Keycloak doesn't support out of the box (OTP, magic links).

---

## 🏗️ Architecture

```
┌──────────────┐        REST         ┌────────────────────┐       Admin API        ┌─────────────┐
│    React     │ ──────────────────▶ │    AsohCloak API    │ ──────────────────────▶│  Keycloak   │
│   Frontend   │                     │  (Resource Server)  │                        │  (Identity  │
└──────────────┘                     └──────────┬───────────┘                       │  Provider)  │
                                                  │                                  └──────┬──────┘
                                                  │                                         │
                                       ┌──────────┴──────────┐                     Custom SPI Provider
                                       │      Data Layer      │                    (OTP + Magic Link)
                                       ├───────────┬──────────┤
                                       │PostgreSQL │  MinIO   │
                                       │(App Data) │(Storage) │
                                       └───────────┴──────────┘
```

- **AsohCloak API** — validates every request as an OAuth2 **resource server**, checking JWTs signed by Keycloak. Never issues or stores tokens itself.
- **Keycloak** — owns registration, login, password resets, blocking/unblocking, and role assignment via its Admin REST API.
- **Custom Keycloak SPI** (`asohcloak-keycloak-providers`, a separate Maven project deployed into Keycloak's `providers/` directory) — extends Keycloak with email OTP and magic-link authenticators, keeping Keycloak as the single source of truth even for flows it doesn't natively support.

---

## ⚙️ Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Version |
|---|---|---|
| ☕ Runtime | Java | 25 |
| 🍃 Framework | Spring Boot | 4.1.1 |
| 🔐 Identity Provider | Keycloak | 26.7.x |
| 🛡️ Security | Spring Security (OAuth2 Resource Server) | — |
| 🗄️ Database | PostgreSQL | 18 |
| 📦 ORM | Spring Data JPA / Hibernate | 7.x |
| 🧬 Migrations | Flyway | 12.7.0 |
| ⚡ Cache / Session Store | Redis | *planned — not yet integrated* |
| 🗺️ Object Mapping | MapStruct | 1.6.3 |
| ✂️ Boilerplate Reduction | Lombok | 1.18.x |
| 📧 Transactional Email | Resend API | — |
| 🪣 Object Storage | MinIO | — |
| 📖 API Docs | springdoc-openapi (Swagger UI) | 3.1.0 |
| 🐳 Containerization | Docker (multi-stage build) | — |
| 🏗️ Build Tool | Maven | — |

