## 🚀 Features

### 🔑 Authentication
- 📝 **Register** — provision a new user through Keycloak
- 🔓 **Login** — issues short-lived access & refresh tokens, only at login
- 🚪 **Logout** — revokes the active session
- 🪄 **Magic Link Login** — passwordless login via emailed one-time link
- 🔢 **OTP Verification** — verify a one-time passcode for 2FA / passwordless flows
- 🔁 **Resend OTP / Magic Link** — request a fresh code or link when the previous one expires

### 🔒 Account Recovery & Lifecycle
- 🔒 **Forgot Password**
- ♻️ **Reset Password**
- ⛔ **Block User** (admin action)
- ✅ **Unblock User** (admin action)

### 🎭 Authorization
- Fine-grained **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)** driven entirely by Keycloak realm roles

---

## 👥 User Roles & RBAC

Roles are defined and assigned inside Keycloak's realm, then enforced in AsohCloak via `@PreAuthorize` checks against the roles embedded in each validated JWT. Typical roles include:

| Role | Description |
|---|---|
| `ADMIN` | Full administrative access (school officials) |
| `BURSAR` | Default role for standard users |

*(This table will grow as School Management roles — e.g. `TEACHER`, `STUDENT` — are introduced.)*

---

## 🛠️ Developer Onboarding

### Prerequisites
- ☕ JDK 25
- 🐳 Docker & Docker Compose
- 📦 Maven (or the bundled `./mvnw` wrapper)
- 🔐 A running Keycloak instance with a configured realm

### Setup

```bash
# 1. Clone the repo
git clone https://github.com/asohyannick/asohCloak.git
cd asohCloak

# 2. Configure environment variables
cp .env.example .env
# fill in real Postgres, Resend, MinIO, and Keycloak values

# 3. Run the app
./mvnw spring-boot:run
```

---

## 🐳 Running with Docker

```bash
docker build -t asohcloak .
docker run --env-file .env -p 8080:8080 asohcloak
```

---

## 🔧 Environment Variables

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `APP_NAME` | Application name used for the Spring context ID |
| `DATABASE_POSTGRESQL_HOST` | Postgres host |
| `DATABASE_POSTGRESQL_PORT` | Postgres port |
| `DATABASE_POSTGRESQL_NAME` | Postgres database name |
| `DATABASE_POSTGRESQL_USER` | Postgres username |
| `DATABASE_POSTGRESQL_PASSWORD` | Postgres password |
| `KEYCLOAK_SERVER_URL` | Base URL of the Keycloak server |
| `KEYCLOAK_REALM` | Keycloak realm name |
| `KEYCLOAK_ISSUER_URI` | Issuer URI used for JWT validation |
| `KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_CLIENT_ID` | Admin API client ID |
| `KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET` | Admin API client secret |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | Resend transactional email API key |
| `RESEND_SENDER_EMAIL` / `RESEND_SENDER_NAME` | Sender identity for outgoing email |
| `MINIO_ENDPOINT`, `MINIO_USERNAME`, `MINIO_PASSWORD`, `MINIO_BUCKET_NAME` | MinIO object storage config |
| `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | Comma-separated list of allowed frontend origins |

Full list lives in `.env.example` — copy it to `.env` and fill in real values. **Never commit `.env`.**

