## 📁 Project Structure

```
src/main/java/com/asohCloak/asohCloak/
├── config/           # Security, Keycloak, and general app configuration
├── controller/        # REST endpoints
├── dto/                # Request/response payloads
├── entity/user/        # JPA entities
├── enums/               # Enum types (e.g. UserRole)
├── exception/            # Custom exceptions + global handler
├── mapper/                # MapStruct mappers
├── repository/             # Spring Data JPA repositories
└── service/                 # Business logic
```

---

## 🔐 Authentication & Security

- Security is delegated **entirely to Keycloak** — no passwords, access tokens, or refresh tokens are minted by this application.
- AsohCloak acts as an **OAuth2 Resource Server**, validating JWTs against Keycloak's JWKS endpoint on every protected request.
- Admin-facing actions (register, block, unblock) go through the **Keycloak Admin REST API** via `keycloak-admin-client`.
- OTP and magic-link flows are implemented as a **custom Keycloak SPI**, kept in a separate project (`asohcloak-keycloak-providers`) since it runs inside the Keycloak server process, not this application.

---

## 📖 API Documentation

Once running, interactive Swagger UI is available at:

```
http://localhost:8080/api/v1/swagger-ui.html
```

---

## 🗄️ Database & Migrations

Schema changes are managed exclusively through **Flyway** — Hibernate's `ddl-auto` is set to `validate` only, never `update` or `create`. Migration files live in `src/main/resources/db/migration/`, named `V{n}__description.sql`. Never edit an already-merged migration; add a new one instead.

---

## 🧪 Testing

```bash
./mvnw clean verify
```

New endpoints should include integration tests covering both authorized and unauthorized access paths.

